            <ArticleTitle>Gangrenous ligamentum teres hepatis causing acute abdominal symptoms.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>267-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This unusual case of a gangrenous round ligament manifested by acute abdominal symptoms underscores the importance of the recent radiologic descriptions of the round ligament in computerized tomography and ultrasonography. The cause of the gangrenous process in this case remains unresolved.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
